  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-02-20T10:20:31.507Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When changing to an avatar that results in a world scale/IPD change, VRChat appears to hold the playspace origin fixed in world space. If the player's HMD position is far from the playspace origin, this change in scale can cause the player to be teleported far from their original location.\n\nThis can cause visible effects even with moderately sized playspaces - I've seen this cause significant displacement about 3m from the origin with ~1m height avatars.\n\nVRChat should instead hold the HMD's XZ coordinates (or possibly the waist tracker, if in 4 or 6-point IK mode) fixed in world space when applying the world scale adjustment.",
